{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward bias in true outcomes vs model: forecasts are systematically too low during rising regimes. Apply a positive level shift (additive uplift) that increases with horizon (small at 1–3d, larger beyond ~5–10d).",
    "Trend underreaction/lag: the model follows recent history too closely and fails to propagate momentum. Add a trend term based on recent slope (e.g., last 5–10d change) to steepen the forward path when slope > 0.",
    "Horizon-specific error growth: underprediction compounds with time; treat error as increasing function of forecast step (e.g., linear ramp uplift from day 1 to day 30).",
    "Post-dip rebound underestimation: after a short-term drawdown in history, the model expects mean reversion down/flat, but realized prices rebound strongly upward. Reduce mean-reversion strength when recent volatility is high and the broader trend is up.",
    "Peak/acceleration miss: during breakout/acceleration phases, the model caps highs (fails to capture convexity). Introduce a convex adjustment (e.g., quadratic or regime switch) when price breaks above recent range/highs."
  ]
}
